{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01C71RiDvTaAvvpYxcK97WuE","input":{"content":"README: correct the Qwen subagent claim against an observed delegation\n\nLive Qwen Code 0.21.5 smoke run, driving a real subagent. It does not work the\nway the adapter's notes claimed.\n\nThe claim was that a `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a\nsub-conversation. What actually happens is that a subagent runs in-process\nbehind an `agent` tool call: no chat file of its own, no `parent_session`\nrecord anywhere in the transcript, so the delegation lands as an ordinary\n`tool_use`/`tool_result` pair in the parent conversation.\n\nNothing is lost by that. The prompt handed to the subagent, its status,\nterminate reason, token counts and a per-tool execution summary all ride in\n`toolCallResult.resultDisplay`, which the adapter preserves in `raw` -- checked\nagainst the captured event, not assumed. But the subagent's own turn-by-turn\nconversation is never written by Qwen at all, only summarised, so no adapter\ncan recover it. That is an upstream limit worth stating plainly rather than a\ngap in this one.\n\nThe `parent_session` mapping is left in place -- it is in Qwen's own\n`KNOWN_RECORD_SUBTYPES` and presumably serves some other sub-session\nmechanism -- but is now labelled as unobserved rather than described as the\nway subagents are captured.\n\nAlso updates the subtype-coverage gap with what live sessions have now\nexercised (`ui_telemetry`, `attribution_snapshot`, `file_history_snapshot`,\n`at_command`, `slash_command`) and records a surprise: `/chat save <title>`\ndoes not emit `custom_title`, it emits two `slash_command` records, so that\npath stays unobserved and may belong to a different gesture entirely.\n\nSmoke-test results behind this commit, all against live CLIs with the hook\ntimeout fixed: the gemini catch-up sweep grew a killed session's stranded tail\n(9 -> 10 events) -- the first time that path has ever run; qwen captured a\nheadless `qwen -p` run; and qwen reported no format drift across 27 events.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg4.txt"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"4fed9c92c790d651bc671f09ab8d881f1641ab11","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-513ac1f31764a738d6d0ffc78e49d7c27ad554e2ffde9a8648a1d31343e7040b","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T02:11:07.313Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01C71RiDvTaAvvpYxcK97WuE","input":{"content":"README: correct the Qwen subagent claim against an observed delegation\n\nLive Qwen Code 0.21.5 smoke run, driving a real subagent. It does not work the\nway the adapter's notes claimed.\n\nThe claim was that a `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a\nsub-conversation. What actually happens is that a subagent runs in-process\nbehind an `agent` tool call: no chat file of its own, no `parent_session`\nrecord anywhere in the transcript, so the delegation lands as an ordinary\n`tool_use`/`tool_result` pair in the parent conversation.\n\nNothing is lost by that. The prompt handed to the subagent, its status,\nterminate reason, token counts and a per-tool execution summary all ride in\n`tool