{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01LdojwdHroSqMgPkuKtEUhA","input":{"content":"qwen-code: attribute a slash command to the human who typed it\n\nA live session recorded `/chat save smoke-test` and `/agents manage` as\n`activity` with actor `system`. Both are keystrokes. Filing them under the\nharness is the ledger recording a person's action as the machine's, and it\ncontradicted the rule the gemini-cli adapter already states for the same class\nof thing -- harness-authored preambles are `system`, slash commands are the\nhuman's, because the human typed them.\n\nThey stay `activity` rather than becoming turns: Qwen marks these\n`sentToModel: false`, so they were never part of the conversation the model\nsaw. What changes is who the ledger says did it.\n\n`RecordContext` grows an optional `identity`, and `recordDraft` applies it when\na record is attributed to `human`, so the event names *which* person the same\nway a turn does. Saying \"a human did this\" while declining to say which one is\nworse than either alternative, and every caller already had the identity in\nhand.\n\nTwo consequences worth stating. `actor` is part of the event identity subset,\nso this re-mints affected events rather than updating them -- a ledger captured\nbefore this change keeps its `system`-attributed copies, and re-capturing adds\n`human` ones beside them. That is inherent to content-addressed append-only\nevents and is acceptable here only because these adapters are unreleased.\n\nAnd it exposes a display question, filed in the Roadmap rather than answered:\n`cledger log` hides the machinery kinds by default, which is right for the 57\n`ui_telemetry` records a real session emits against 45 events of content, but\nwrong for a slash command a person typed -- the default keys on the kind, not\non whose action it was. Capture is unaffected either way; everything is\nrecorded and `cledger export` stays lossless. The fix worth trying is to key\nthe default on the actor, which `activity` now carries for exactly this reason.\n\nAlso corrects the Roadmap's DETACH_SUFFIX entry, which still repeated the\nmechanism that reading both CLIs' sources disproved.\n\nTests: 204, 203 pass / 1 pre-existing skip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg5.txt"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"4fed9c92c790d651bc671f09ab8d881f1641ab11","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-e34a6338d8a4f5926ad8bef0bcf71e740476d603423895ff2237eaf8ed51340c","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T02:19:43.581Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01LdojwdHroSqMgPkuKtEUhA","input":{"content":"qwen-code: attribute a slash command to the human who typed it\n\nA live session recorded `/chat save smoke-test` and `/agents manage` as\n`activity` with actor `system`. Both are keystrokes. Filing them under the\nharness is the ledger recording a person's action as the machine's, and it\ncontradicted the rule the gemini-cli adapter already states for the same class\nof thing -- harness-authored preambles are `system`, slash commands are the\nhuman's, because the human typed them.\n\nThey stay `activity` rather than becoming tu