{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All five tests are done. Pushed as `990bdf1`.\n\n## Results\n\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 1 — Gemini model turns + tool calls | ✅ pass, no double-emitted calls |\n| 2 — `/rewind` | ✅ pass, union capture holds |\n| 3 — catch-up sweep | ✅ **pass** — `9 → 10`, first time that path has ever run |\n| 4 — Qwen kinds | ✅ pass on capture and **no format drift**; two FAILs explained below |\n| 5 — Qwen headless | ✅ pass, `23 → 27` events |\n\n## Your two Test 4 \"failures\" were both my checker being wrong, not the adapter\n\n**`/chat save` doesn't emit `custom_title`.** It emits two `slash_command` records with `rawCommand: \"/chat save smoke-test\"`. The adapter filed them correctly as `activity`. My checker asserted a mapping that came from Qwen's subtype *list*, not from observed behaviour — so `custom_title` remains unobserved and may belong to some other gesture entirely. Recorded as such.\n\n**Your subagent finding is the valuable one, and the PR's claim was wrong.** Thank you for pushing past `/agents` — that's what exposed it.\n\nThe PR said \"a `parent_session` record makes a subagent chat a sub-conversation.\" That is not how Qwen 0.21.5 works. A subagent runs **in-process behind an `agent` tool call** — no chat file of its own, no `parent_session` record anywhere. So the delegation lands as an ordinary `tool_use`/`tool_result` pair in the parent.\n\nI checked what survives, rather than assuming:\n\n```\nraw.data.toolCallResult.resultDisplay preserved? YES\n  subagent taskPrompt preserved?  YES\n  subagent toolUsage preserved?   YES\n```\n\nSo the prompt you handed the subagent, its status, terminate reason, token counts and per-tool execution summary are all in the ledger. But the subagent's **own turn-by-turn conversation is never written by Qwen at all** — only summarised (`toolUsage: [{name: read_file, count: 1}]`). That's an upstream limit no adapter can work around, and it's now stated plainly instead of being papered over.\n\n## One decision I'd like from you\n\nYour `slash_command` records land like this:\n\n```\nkind=activity actor=system rawCommand=\"/chat save smoke-test\"\nkind=activity actor=system rawCommand=\"/agents manage\"\n```\n\n**You typed those, but they're attributed to `system` and hidden from the default `cledger log` view.** Meanwhile the Gemini adapter explicitly attributes slash commands to the human, on the reasoning that the human typed them. So the two adapters disagree about the same class of thing.\n\nNothing is lost either way — `rawCommand` is preserved verbatim. It's a question of attribution and visibility, and it's a semantics change to recorded data, so I'd rather you called it than have me quietly pick.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"4fed9c92c790d651bc671f09ab8d881f1641ab11","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-2327cc3d8b1e769e91a41cd18636080d843214f4d41d98ce8f48aa63eca84de7","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T02:11:39.755Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"All five tests are done. Pushed as `990bdf1`.\n\n## Results\n\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 1 — Gemini model turns + tool calls | ✅ pass, no double-emitted calls |\n| 2 — `/rewind` | ✅ pass, union capture holds |\n| 3 — catch-up sweep | ✅ **pass** — `9 → 10`, first time that path has ever run |\n| 4 — Qwen kinds | ✅ pass on capture and **no format dri