{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Done, pushed as `4fed9c9`. All 204 tests pass (203 + the pre-existing skip).\n\n## On your red flag — you were half right, and the half you were right about matters\n\nLet me be precise, because I was sloppy earlier. **Hiding is purely a display default. Nothing is withheld from the record.** Every `ui_telemetry` ping, every slash command, every file snapshot is captured, stored, and comes out of `cledger export` losslessly. `--with-state` only changes what `cledger log` prints. So cledger is not deciding what to record — your principle already holds where it counts.\n\nBut your instinct pointed at something real anyway. **The default keys on the *kind*, not on *whose action it was*.** That's why a slash command you typed was hidden by the same rule as a token-count ping. Those aren't the same thing, and the rule can't tell them apart.\n\nThe default itself earns its keep — one of your real Qwen sessions emitted **57 `ui_telemetry` records against 45 events of actual content**, so an unfiltered `log` would bury the conversation. The problem isn't that there's a filter; it's where the line is drawn.\n\nSo yes, worth a TODO, and it's now in the Roadmap with the fix I'd try: **key the default on the actor rather than the kind** — show human-driven records, keep harness and agent bookkeeping behind the flag. That's newly possible precisely because of the change you just approved: `activity` now carries a real actor.\n\n## What #1 changed\n\n```\nbefore:  kind=activity actor=system  rawCommand=\"/chat save smoke-test\"\nafter:   kind=activity actor=human   rawCommand=\"/chat save smoke-test\"\n```\n\nThey stay `activity` rather than becoming turns, because Qwen marks them `sentToModel: false` — the model never saw them. And the event now names *which* human (`actor.id = your git email`), since \"a human did this\" without saying who is worse than either alternative.\n\nOne consequence I should flag plainly: `actor` is part of the event identity hash, so re-capturing **minted new events beside the old ones** rather than updating them — your smoke ledger now has both copies. That's inherent to content-addressed append-only events, and acceptable only because these adapters are unreleased. If this had shipped, the old attribution would be permanent.\n\n## Where the PR stands\n\nSix commits. All five smoke tests pass. Four real bugs fixed (dead sweep, rewinding cursor, unrecorded snapshot drops, the 120ms timeout), plus two documented claims that turned out to be false — the `DETACH_SUFFIX` mechanism and the Qwen subagent story — both of which only surfaced because you drove the CLIs by hand.\n\nThe PR is still marked draft. Want me to update the PR description to reflect all of this and mark it ready?","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"4fed9c92c790d651bc671f09ab8d881f1641ab11","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-1fa32dbd2d917ec851e7969e6802cc568e27ab522919dc39d4778e9601f77b3c","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T02:20:14.511Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Done, pushed as `4fed9c9`. All 204 tests pass (203 + the pre-existing skip).\n\n## On your red flag — you were half right, and the half you were right about matters\n\nLet me be precise, because I was sloppy earlier. **Hiding is purely a display default. Nothing is withheld from the record.** Every `ui_telemet